WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
Good morning John!

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:05.160
So here's a thing that I don't think Nerdfighters
need to be told, but maybe you know, subconsciously

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.360
even if you don't think about it, because
I don't really think about it but it's definitely

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.140
a choice I make every single video.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.010
Some videos I make because I want as many
people as possible to see them.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:16.460
Whether that's to get a lot of views because
it feels good, or to grow the community, or

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.960
to convey an idea that I feel like more people
need to have in their heads.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.200
And some videos are just for Nerdfighters.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.370
Just for the people who are gonna watch no
matter what, as long as I don't just sit here

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.110
and do nothing for four minutes.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.730
And I gotta say, I really like those videos.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:34.469
I like not having the pressure; I like just
being able to talk about what's in my head.

00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:39.100
Also this community has given me so many wonderful
gifts; I like to give you guys gifts back.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.920
I'll do a lot of things for you guys.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.359
Do you wanna see me lick a battery?

00:00:43.359 --> 00:00:44.649
A-AH-Ahhh.

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:46.789
I connected the positive and the negative.

00:00:46.789 --> 00:00:47.789
Science.

00:00:47.789 --> 00:00:50.340
[distorted voice] Maybe it'd be better if
I just made the entire video with this thing!

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.290
Probably not.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:55.460
[spitting noise]

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:59.300
It's weird to feel in debt to a lot of people
and not know how to pay that debt back.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.079
One of the ways I feel like I could do it
is just to make videos for you that nobody

00:01:02.079 --> 00:01:05.860
else is gonna see and it's clearly just for
the people who've been so supportive of us.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.560
And also I feel like it's good th--to like
define what the community of Nerdfighteria

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.570
is every once in a while, 'cause I think some
people don't really understand.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.350
I mean I don't think that anybody really understands
it.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.159
But I did just get an ask from somebody on
Tumblr who said that they'd been shamed in

00:01:17.159 --> 00:01:20.200
a Nerdfighter community for being transgender,
and, like, what?

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:24.031
I don't know how someone could feel like that's
the kinda thing a Nerdfighter would do, but

00:01:24.031 --> 00:01:25.031
it's not.

00:01:25.031 --> 00:01:27.460
That's--you're--that's not a Ner--that's not
a Nerdfighter.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:30.770
So sometimes I worry about what this all is
and that people are doing the wrong things

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:34.280
in the name of the thing, and not understanding
the thing.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.799
And I also worry about the decoupling of productivity
and wages.

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:40.979
Productivity is just all the benefits to humans
that the economy creates.

00:01:40.979 --> 00:01:43.859
And wages, of course, are the money that people
make.

00:01:43.859 --> 00:01:47.630
And they used to be things that were really
closely tied together, and now... they're

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:48.630
not anymore.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.030
I'm worried about what this means for our
society: that the rich are just gonna get

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:54.200
richer, and that the poor aren't gonna benefit,
and it's gonna create instability as well

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.200
as suffering.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.890
And I'm also worried about what the world's
gonna look like if we're able to create lots

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:00.789
of cool services for people, and they're gonna
be so cheap that maybe people don't even need

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:03.469
to pay for them, like, what does that world
look like?

00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:06.350
I wanna make a video on this topic, a video
that lots of people, not just Nerdfighters

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.350
would watch...

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.610
But I'm no econonomist, so I gotta do a bunch
of research and learn stuff...

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:12.330
Like, like how to pronounce econonomist.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.420
Also, VidCon's coming up.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.390
I'm not worried about VidCon in general.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:18.692
There's lots of cool things that--like amazing
things that're gonna happen at VidCon, like,

00:02:18.692 --> 00:02:19.880
it's gonna be a good time.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:23.200
But we're having this meet-and-greet lottery
thing, if you wanna go to--into the signing

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.610
hall and get any signings or pictures and
anything you gotta do the lottery, you gotta

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:30.690
rank all your favorite creators, how much
you like them and then the system assigns

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:31.690
you meet-and-greets.

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:33.580
And if you don't do the lottery thing, you
don't get any.

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:38.280
And so far only about half of people who have
registered have signed up for the lottery,

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:42.001
and that terrifies me, because I feel like,
maybe they just don't know it's a thing.

00:02:42.001 --> 00:02:45.670
And maybe I'm living in this old-person world
where people check their email, and they don't

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:49.010
check their email, and I don't know how to
get in touch with people who don't check their

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.010
email!

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.870
So I'm worried about people showing up at
VidCon and being very disappointed because

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:56.010
they did not sign up for the lottery.... but
I don't know what to do about that problem.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:57.590
So those are some things I've been worried
about...

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:58.890
Here's some things I'm excited about!

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:02.400
I produce multiple YouTube shows and what
producing means, I'm not really sure.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.260
One of those shows is called How To Adult,
which is fairly self-explanatory.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:09.390
And it's very useful, even for me, a guy who's
been adult-ing for, like, 15 years.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:13.730
How To Adult is launching its Patreon page
today to help pay for its existence, so if

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:17.590
you're interested in learning "how to adult,"
or you already like How To Adult and you wanna

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.250
help them continue making cool stuff...

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.420
You can check that stuff out, link's in the
description.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.090
I'm also producing a new show with Charlie
McDonnell, uh, called Cereal Time.

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:28.570
It's a morning show, five days a week.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.220
It's a lot like Good Mythical Morning, but
it's more British.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:33.540
And I'm excited about doing more things with
Nerdfighteria.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:34.540
Doin' stuff together.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.290
Like, I--I wanna do a scavenger hunt.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:37.680
So I'm gonna be thinkin' about that.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:38.840
And maybe you can help.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.660
But I'm not gonna tell you how to help, cause
I already did.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:44.760
Thank you to all the people who watched this
video because I know that you are among the

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:49.820
people who watch them no matter what, every
single one, and that means a lot to me.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.540
Thanks... for being a part of this!

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.040
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

